  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Fredskommunikations projekt                       &quot;World&#xB4;s largest conversation&quot;</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peace Communication Project                       &quot;World&#xB4;s largest conversation&quot; - &quot;World&#xB4;s largest conversation&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Internationella Organisationen f&#xF6;r Migration (IOM) har ans&#xF6;kt om finansiering f&#xF6;r att genomf&#xF6;ra projektet &#x201C;World&#xB4;s Largest Conversation&#x201D;. Projektets syfte &#xE4;r att uppmuntra civilt deltagande och &#xF6;ppen debatt under &#xF6;verg&#xE5;ngen till ett post-konfliktscenario och fredsbyggnadsprocessen p&#xE5; landsbygden. J&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet och milj&#xF6; kommer utg&#xF6;ra tv&#xE5; viktiga teman. Projektet har tre faser: (1) en medvetandeg&#xF6;randekampanj f&#xF6;r att folk ska k&#xE4;nna till initiativet och hur de kan delta, (2) st&#xF6;d och diskussion p&#xE5; de platser dialogerna &#xE4;ger rum och (3) civil deltagande f&#xF6;r att fr&#xE4;mja fred. N&#xE4;r det g&#xE4;ller resultat p&#xE5; impact-niv&#xE5; &#xE5;r projektets m&#xE5;l att 1 % av befolkningen i de 32 kommunerna och 14 storst&#xE4;derna k&#xE4;nner till kommunikationssatsningen och dess verksamhetsf&#xE4;lt.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LCMGDM is a social mobilization and education plan designed by a working group (the &#x201C;Pedagogy Group for Peace- GPP&#x201D;) within the Minister Counselor for Communications of the Presidency to encourage citizen participation and public deliberation during the transition to a post-conflict scenario and the territorial peace building process. The project has three phases: (1) an awareness campaign for people to know about the initiative and how they can participate, (2) support and deliberation where the dialogues take place and (3) civil mobilization in favour of peace. Gender and Environment will be two fundamental issues. As to the impact result, the project aims at achieving that 1% of the population from the 32 municipalities and 14 capital cities recognize LCMGDM and its spaces.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LCMGDM is  visible in 32 municipalities and 14 capital cities as an experience of social mobilisation and peace pedagogy that encourage citizen participation and public deliberation through a diverse series of dialogues on issues related to the conflict and collective peace building process.</narrative>
  </description>
